{title: Close to Thee}
{artist: Fanny Crosby / Silas J. Vail}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: G}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The United Methodist Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: United Methodist Publishing House, 1989), # 407)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Thou my ever[D]lasting [G]portion,
[G]More than friend or life to [D]me,
[G]All along my pilgrim [C]journey,
[C]Savior, [G]let me walk with Thee.
[D7]Close to Thee, close to [G]Thee,
[G]Close to Thee, close to [D]Thee,
[G]All along my pilgrim [C]journey,
[C]Savior, [G]let me walk with Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Not for ease or [D]worldly [G]pleasure,
[G]Nor for fame my prayer [D]shall [G]be;
[G]Gladly will I toil [C]and suffer,
[C]Only [G]let me walk with Thee.
[D7]Close to Thee, close to [G]Thee,
[G]Close to Thee, close to [D]Thee,
[G]Gladly will I toil and [C]suffer,
[C]Only [G]let me walk with Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Lead me through the [D]vale of [G]shadows,
[G]Bear me over life’s fitful [D]sea;
[G]Then the gate of life e[C]ternal
[C]May I [G]enter, Lord, with Thee.
[D7]Close to Thee, close to [G]Thee,
[G]Close to Thee, close to [D]Thee,
[G]Then the gate of life e[C]ternal
[C]May I [G]enter, Lord, with Thee.
{end_of_verse}
